> Well, the bee thing makes sense, since real bees are (with some
> exceptions, I think) hatched into their role and can't ever change it:
> A queen is a queen and a drone is a drone from before it's even a
> larvae. Most bees in a hive are neuter anyway, I think. (cue apiarist
> pedantry from someone who knows their bees).

Worker bees are sterile females, afaik. Drones are male, queens are
fertile females. The sterile/fertile distinction is apparently an
effect of the food the larva receives; there's no way to change them
from one to the other once the imago (adult insect) has hatched.

> the wizard/shaman thing
> kind of makes sense too, since an orc captain lacks all the magical
> abilities of an orc shaman.

Orcish, gnomish and kobold spellcasters are magic-users and as such
have access to the same spell list as major liches: if you're silly
enough to feed a kobold shaman 20+ potions of gain level, the piddly
shaman can touch-of-death you or summon nasties.

